    "text": "This report details the Office of Inspector General's Spring 2026 - Semiannual Report to Congress.  \n\n \n\n \n\nU.S. Small Business Administration - Office of Inspector General (SBA-OIG) [ https://www.sba.gov/about-sba/oversight-advocacy/office-inspector-general?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \n \n \n \n \n\nU.S. Small Business Administration, Office of Inspector General's Spring 2026 - Semiannual Report to Congress [ https://www.sba.gov/document/report-semiannual-report-congress?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\n\nToday, the U.S. Small Business Administration (SBA), Office of Inspector General (OIG) is pleased to present the Spring 2026 - Semiannual Report to Congress. This report summarizes OIG’s activities from October 1, 2025 through March 31, 2026.\n\nYou may read the report by *CLICKING HERE [ https://www.sba.gov/document/report-semiannual-report-congress?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*.\n\nDuring this reporting period, OIG continued to bring fraudsters to justice and provide a significant return on investment to American taxpayers. During the 6-month period from October 2025 through March 2026, OIG issued 8 audit reports with 13 recommendations to improve SBA operations and mitigate fraud and unnecessary losses in agency programs. We questioned $32 billion in costs from our oversight reviews. In addition, OIG investigations resulted in 83 indictments, 52 convictions, and over $244 million in dollar accomplishments — bringing our total monetary accomplishments to about $32.3 billion.\n\nThe nation can depend on OIG to provide independent, objective, and timely oversight of SBA. OIG’s engaged workforce will continue to give taxpayers a significant return on investment, rooting out fraud, waste, and abuse in SBA programs.\n\n*Share This Report* [ https://www.sba.gov/document/report-semiannual-report-congress?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n \n\nReport fraud, waste, abuse, mismanagement, or misconduct \ninvolving SBA programs or employees.\n\n*Submit a Complaint* [ https://www.sba.gov/about-sba/oversight-advocacy/office-inspector-general/office-inspector-general-hotline?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \n \n \n\n \n \nU.S. Small Business Administration\n*Office of Inspector General*  409 3rd St. SW, Suite 7150\nWashington, DC 20416 sba.gov/oig [ https://www.sba.gov/about-sba/oversight-advocacy/office-inspector-general?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/u-s-small-business-administration-office-of-inspector-general/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/SBAOIG?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Subscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USSBAOIG/subscriber/new ]  \n \n Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USSBAOIG/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]  \n \n \n\n________________________________________________________________________\n\n This email was sent to jish.nath@cloudbaud.com using govDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Small Business Administration - Office of Inspector General (SBA-OIG) · 409 3rd St., SW · Washington, DC 20416 GovDelivery logo  [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \n \nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;} p, li, h1, h2, h3 { overflow-wrap: normal; word-wrap: normal; word-break: keep-all; -moz-hyphens: none; -ms-hyphens: none; -webkit-hyphens: none; hyphens: none; mso-hyphenate: none; }\n",
